Night sweep November 2 2026, fired at 03:00 MST six hours after the evening pass. The mcp.so recentServers block carried 30 cards with a date and the newest at 2026-11-02T09:04:11Z, so two sat above the evening stamp of 2026-11-02T01:54:34Z: docuwriter-ai and signal8. The mcpservers.org /all read behaved as the two prior passes recorded, the first fetch returning 18,883, the same counter and the same thirty slugs the evening pass dispositioned, and the second fetch cache-busted with a nanosecond stamp and a changed user agent returning 18,885 with the page turned over, so the read whose counter moves is the live one and the read that repeats the previous counter is a proxy snapshot. Two arrivals were catalogued. Catalogian MCP was driven end to end with no account: POST /v1/ephemeral/ingest with a URL returned a session token good for twenty four hours, three ingests and fifty tool calls, initialize answered 200 with serverInfo catalogian 1.1.0, tools/list returned 18 read-only tools in 28,237 bytes, a public building permit dataset ingested as 300 rows and 117 fields under key field id with truncated false, snapshot_schema returned field types with null rates and example values, query_snapshot group_by on permit_type answered 299 and 1 in one object, filter_snapshot_rows on contains SIGNS returned the single matching row, search_snapshot for electric returned rows ranked by relevance, a second ingest at a different slice landed on the same record with a delta of 100 new and 100 deleted and 200 unchanged recorded as edition 2 kind revision and returned at row level by get_edition_diff, download_snapshot failed with an S3 signature mismatch and compare_snapshots answered Removed 0 on the same edge where get_delta answered deletedCount 100, and a vendor sample file with a byte order mark produced a key field taken as the BOM prefixed ID and then a KEY_FIELD_MISSING refusal on headers that visibly contain the column, while an ingest of a CSV with no accepted key column